::MCR_U03_L03_Quiz_Q01::
Question ID: MCR_U03_L03_Quiz_Q01
MLA Standard: Readiness Support Only - Extension of MLA.MCR.DL.2 and MLA.MCR.DL.4
Question:
Which action best supports comparing two data sets responsibly: compare medians to describe center?
{
=A. Use the data feature named in the question and explain it in context.#Correct. A responsible comparison uses the stated data feature and connects it to the context.
~B. Ignore the spread and choose the higher maximum.#This focuses on one value and misses the full distribution.
~C. Choose the set that looks more interesting.#This is opinion, not data-based reasoning.
~D. Make a claim without naming the data sets.#A comparison must name and describe the data sets clearly.
}
